    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1104-a1">

                <pb facs="1030" n="772" xml:id="pg772"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 1]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">British Consulate General</hi>, <lb/>
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New York</hi></placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-11-01">_ _ _ _ _ _ _</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: With reference to your letter of _ _
                    _ _ _ _ _ with regard to enlistment in His Majesty’s forces, I have to inform
                    you that this office is not authorised to furnish free passages from the United
                    States to England to British subjects who wish to return for the purpose of
                    enlisting.</p>
                <p>British subjects however who are willing to work their way to England can as a
                    rule obtain employment without remuneration as horse attendants on
                    homeward-bound vessels. A gratuity of one pound is usually given to such
                    attendants on arrival in England in return for their services. If you wish to
                    take advantage of this method of returning home, you should notify this office
                    accordingly.</p>
                <p>Thanking you for your patriotic offer, I am [etc.]</p>
            </div>
        </body>
